2026-10-30T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2349) 'How the house recorder writes CineForm
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2349) 'The house recorder's current release ships the `cfhd` CineForm
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2349) 'encoder. Its custom output, built on FFmpeg, is set to Matroska with
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2349) '`cfhd` video and FLAC audio. In a still-frame test every frame decoded
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2349) 'through the CineForm SDK at 39.4 dB against the input. The control,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2349) 'the same input shifted 40 px, scored 16.3 dB.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2349) 'Encoding outside the house recorder
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2349) 'A render that is not a live capture encodes with the CineForm SDK
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2349) 'through the engine's CineForm module or the CineForm interactor.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2349) 'Delivery uses the AV1-in-Matroska interactor's `deliver.exs`. It
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2349) 'rewraps the frames byte for byte and checks every frame and sample.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2349) '- A render reel records through the engine's movie writer straight to
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2349) '  CineForm. It writes no PNG frames to encode later (operator,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2349) '  2026-10-17).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2349) '- Large media and videos are kept on the Windows desk, not on the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2349) '  Mac mini, which sits on a remote network (operator, 2026-10-17). A
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2349) '  render made on the Mac is copied to the desk, its size is read back
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2349) '  there, and only then is the Mac copy deleted.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2349) 'How a file is checked
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2349) '`deliver.exs` checks every frame and every sample. `av1mkv dump-frame`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2349) 'pulls frames, and a person looks at them. The run's length is gated
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2349) 'from the frames' own timestamps, and a short frame set is the control
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2349) 'that must fail. The frames and samples are the check, whatever exit
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2349) 'code the recorder returns.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2349  1 LINE
 Text:Written

